"Summarizes each time interval with opening and closing values inside a body and full observed high–low wicks.\n\nUse when: Ordered intervals contain meaningful open, high, low, and close measurements. Within-interval direction and range matter together.\n\nAvoid when: The four summaries are unavailable or opening and closing have no domain meaning.\n\nVisual grammar: Horizontal position identifies the time interval. Body endpoints encode open and close; wick endpoints encode high and low; fill indicates direction.\n\nBuild: Aggregate records into explicit intervals using correct time zones and market sessions. Draw a body spanning open to close with a thin high–low wick. Explain positive/negative body styling and keep a readable value scale.\n\nCheck: Check low is no greater than open, close, or high. Verify high is no less than both open and close. Confirm missing intervals and closed periods have a documented spacing policy.\n\nPitfalls: A candle hides the order of price movements inside its interval. Red and green alone are inaccessible; pair fill differences with outlines or other consistent styling.\n\nExample: Show synthetic daily auction prices for twenty sessions with opening/closing bodies and high–low wicks.\n\nAlternatives: Range bar chart, Line chart, Box plot."
